json SlotGameInfoR {
    doc """
    The Brave Slots machine definition, as stored in
    deploy/system/brave_slots.json.

    THIS IS THE STORAGE SHAPE, NOT THE WIRE SHAPE.  It is serialized into
    SlotgameInfoResp, whose C38FmiUn is a JSON STRING - see there.
    """

    field info type="SlotGameInfo" {
        key "C38FmiUn"
        doc "Machine configuration: id, name, reel positions, the medal it spends, sprite list, help url."
    }

    field pictures type="[SlotGamePictureInfo]" {
        key "rY6j0Jvs"
        doc "The reel symbols, by picture id."
    }
}

json SlotgameInfoResp {
    doc """
    The Brave Slots definition ON THE WIRE, keyed C7J9hbmr
    (SlotgameInfoResponse).

    ⚠ TWO things about this shape are not guessable, and getting either wrong
    leaves SlotgameStandInfo empty - which is silent, because the handler still
    "succeeds":

    1. THE ROOT KEY IS C7J9hbmr, NOT C38FmiUn.  GameResponseParser::
       getResponseObject dispatches on C7J9hbmr; C38FmiUn is a FIELD inside it
       and appears nowhere in that table.  Emitting the inner struct is the
       handbook 6.11 wrapper trap, and it is what we shipped until 2026-08-21:
       the client could not dispatch the reply at all, so the slot machine ran
       on default data and RandallSlotActionScene::downloadFiles asked for no
       sprites, because getSlotgameInfo()->getSlotImage() had nothing in it.

    2. C38FmiUn IS A JSON STRING, not a nested object.  readParam @0x1447E5C
       runs strlen() then picojson::parse() over the value and looks the inner
       fields up in the resulting map, so the whole SlotGameInfo has to be
       serialized and embedded as one string.
    """

    field game_info type=str {
        key "C38FmiUn"
        doc "SlotGameInfo serialized to JSON and embedded AS A STRING.  The client picojson-parses it (readParam @0x1447EA8)."
    }

    field pictures type="[SlotGamePictureInfo]" {
        key "rY6j0Jvs"
        doc "The reel symbols."
    }

    field reels type="[SlotGameReelInfo]" {
        key "iW62Scdg"
        doc "Reel definitions.  The third field SlotgameInfoResponse handles; we have no data for it yet, so it goes out empty."
    }
}

json ControlCenterEnterResp {
    doc """
    ControlCenterEnter (uYF93Mhc) response.

    Fired by LoginScene and RandallSummonScene - NOT by any Slots scene - but
    it is what seeds SlotgameStandInfo, because getResponseObject is a global
    key->class registry (handbook 7.12.4): any response carrying C7J9hbmr
    populates the client's slot state regardless of which handler sent it.  So
    the machine is configured at login, long before the tile is opened.
    """

    field slotgame type="SlotgameInfoResp" {
        key "C7J9hbmr"
        doc "The Brave Slots machine definition."
    }
}

